{"qid":"Q1241847","names":["Giudicato of Arborea"],"title":"Giudicato of Arborea","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Giudicato of Arborea was one of four indigenous Sardinian kingdoms that emerged from the fragmentation of Byzantine administration by the ninth century, occupying the central-western part of the island centered on Oristano. Under Marianus IV (1353–1375) Arborea drove back Aragonese expansion and reconquered most of Sardinia, and his daughter Eleanor of Arborea (regent from 1387) codified the Carta de Logu, a legal corpus granting notable protections that remained in force until 1827. After Eleanor's death in 1404 the kingdom weakened; the Aragonese victory at the Battle of Sanluri (1409) broke its military power, and Alfonso V purchased the remaining noble claims for 100,000 gold florins in 1420, completing Aragonese control of Sardinia.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The Giudicato's territory is reasonably well mapped from medieval Sardinian documents and Aragonese administrative records, and its final boundaries before absorption are among the best-attested of the four judicates.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Judicate of Arborea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judicate_of_Arborea"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Eleanor of Arborea","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eleanor_of_Arborea"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Battle of Sanluri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Sanluri"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Judicate of Arborea","rulers":[{"qid":"Q2279633","name":"Gonario I of Lacon Gunale","start":1015,"end":1038,"image":null},{"qid":"Q2279550","name":"B